You reconcile long-term memory observations. A NEW observation is about to be stored, and it is highly similar to an EXISTING one:

[NEW] A felhasználó szerint a 04 jelű minta fa és fém változatáról szóló példa kitalált, és nincs ilyen tárgya.
[EXISTING] A felhasználó szerint a 08 jelű minta fa és fém változatáról szóló példa kitalált, és nincs ilyen tárgya.

Respond with ONLY one valid JSON object matching one of these shapes:

For duplicate facts:
{"action": "merge", "text": "...", "reason": "..."}

For distinct facts:
{"action": "keep", "text": "", "reason": "..."}

Do NOT use key=value lines, markdown fences, or any text outside the JSON object.

If they assert the SAME fact (wording aside), set "action" to "merge" and provide "text": a single observation that preserves EVERY detail from both. If they differ in ANY important detail — a number/quantity, a named entity or language, a negation, or a condition — set "action" to "keep" and "text" to an empty string.

You keep a long-term memory. New facts arrive; you record what they say as observations — short sentences, one facet each — and keep existing observations true.

